# Line endings are pinned to LF for everything textual.
#
# This is written from Windows, and git's default would convert LF to CRLF on checkout. That is harmless for
# the .mjs files but not for the rest: a CRLF `run: |` block in a GitHub Actions workflow breaks under bash
# (the trailing \r becomes part of the command), and a CRLF Dockerfile RUN line can do the same inside the
# image. The container and CI are Linux; the repository should look like it.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Belt and braces for the files where a stray \r actually breaks something.
*.mjs      text eol=lf
*.json     text eol=lf
*.md       text eol=lf
*.css      text eol=lf
*.yml      text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
.env.example text eol=lf

# Never touched by end-of-line conversion.
*.db       binary
*.sqlite   binary
*.png      binary
*.ico      binary
